    "answer": {
      "short": "For example, $2$ and $3$.",
      "worked": "$2$ and $3$ are both prime, and $2+3=5$, which is odd. More generally, $2$ and any other prime number work because $2$ is the only even prime and an even number plus an odd number is odd.",
